messages:
maria: FYI I opened PR #842 to add a tiny telemetry example to the Optimize toolkit docs. It shows how to record batching and KV cache hit rates using Prometheus + the SDK. Would love a quick docs review and link-check. https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/842

devops-bot: PR opened by maria in docs repo — reviewers requested: @ashwin @kenji

ashwin: Dropping by to review. Is this intended for the migration guide or the quickstart examples page? I think quickstart makes more sense for snippets.

maria: Quickstart. The migration guide will get a separate appendix later. This snippet is intentionally minimal — just counters and a sample histogram for batch size.

kenji: Can you add a tiny JS snippet too? Most SDK examples are python-first and we should keep parity.

maria: Good call. I added a JS sample in the PR, under the 'Examples' section. Code is below:

```js
// minimal SDK telemetry example
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood.Client({ apiKey: process.env.RW_KEY });
const batchHistogram = new client.metrics.Histogram('opt.batch_size');
const cacheHits = new client.metrics.Counter('opt.kv_cache_hits');

async function callModel(inputs) {
  batchHistogram.observe(inputs.length);
  // ... request logic
  const res = await client.generate({ model: 'redwood/sm-quant', inputs });
  if (res.meta.cacheHit) cacheHits.inc();
  return res;
}
```

sara: Heads-up the PR contains a link to an internal eval harness (docs/internal/eval-harness.md) — linter flagged it as a broken public link. We should either remove the link or add a redirect page.

maria: Thanks — I removed the internal link and replaced it with a public 'evaluations overview' page. Please re-run the doc linter.

ashwin: Quick nit: the quant profile example in the PR uses 'sm-quant' — can we add a short note about precision tradeoffs and link to the quantization profiles doc? Otherwise folks will copy-paste with no context.

maria: Added a one-paragraph note and a link to /docs/optimize/quantization-profiles. Also included a tiny table of recommended profiles for latency-sensitive vs cost-sensitive workloads.

kenji: LGTM modulo the linter. @docs-bot can you run the docs CI? :eyes:

docs-bot: Docs CI queued for PR #842 — lint, linkcheck, build (expected ~6m)

sara: If the linkcheck passes, I'm happy to merge after a couple of wording tweaks. I left inline comments on phrasing in the Python snippet.

maria: Awesome — thanks everyone. I'll address wording now and push one more commit. :thumbsup:

ashwin: When you update, can you also add a short note on the expected metric cardinality? We want to avoid high-cardinality label usage in sample snippets.

maria: Good call, added a comment in both snippets about label design (keep labels low-cardinality, don't include request IDs).

kenji: Perfect. Once CI is green and lint fixes are addressed, feel free to merge. :shipit:

maria: Merged after CI green at 2076543330 — thanks all!
